From: basanos doom staged-sweep worker
Subject: [PATCH 0014] zero PU_LEVSPEC zone blocks so ST1 commits no stale bytes

EV_DoPlat leaves plat_t.count unset until the lift reaches a stop and
EV_DoDoor/EV_VerticalDoor leave vldoor_t.topcountdown unset until the door
reaches the top.  The recycled zone block keeps stale bytes (measured:
pointer bits that differ between host processes) and ST1 v0 encodes every
field, so the committed state carried non-semantic garbage for the life of
such a thinker (measured: 160 tics of DEMO1 from tic 597).  Every such field
is written before it is read, so zeroing PU_LEVSPEC blocks changes no play.

--- a/linuxdoom-1.10/z_zone.c
+++ b/linuxdoom-1.10/z_zone.c
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 rcsid[] = "$Id: z_zone.c,v 1.4 1997/02/03 16:47:58 b1 Exp $";
 
 #include <stdint.h>
+#include <string.h>
 
 #include "z_zone.h"
 #include "i_system.h"
@@ -300,6 +301,17 @@
     mainzone->rover = base->next;	
 	
     base->id = ZONEID;
+
+    /* Special thinkers (doors, plats, floors, ceilings, lights) are
+       allocated PU_LEVSPEC and vanilla leaves some fields unset until
+       first use (plat_t.count until the lift reaches a stop, vldoor_t
+       .topcountdown until the door reaches the top).  The recycled zone
+       block then holds stale bytes, often pointer bits, which the ST1
+       codec commits.  Zero them: every such field is written before it is
+       read, so play is unchanged and ST1 becomes a function of game state
+       on every build. */
+    if (tag == PU_LEVSPEC)
+	memset ((byte *)base + sizeof(memblock_t), 0, base->size - sizeof(memblock_t));
     
     return (void *) ((byte *)base + sizeof(memblock_t));
 }
